d 'EQUIPOP': module to construct individualized population-based spatial contexts
d
d  equipop constructs individualized, or bespoke, spatial contexts
d around every observation in a georeferenced dataset. Its
d distinctive feature is that neighbourhood size can be set by
d accumulated reference population rather than by a fixed number of
d rows or a common geographical radius: an observation representing
d 600 people contributes 600 towards a requested k, so the distance
d needed to reach k varies with local density. The command returns
d that geographical reach together with contextual population
d totals and, when requested, group counts and shares. Several
d population thresholds and fixed radii may be evaluated in one
d call. Optional distance decay supports negative-exponential,
d exponential-normal, exponential-square-root, log-normal and power
d families, with a common bandwidth or one that varies across
d observations. Further options control grid resolution, treatment
d of the origin cell, allocation of population at the neighbourhood
d boundary and coordinate projection. 
d
d KW: spatial contexts
d KW: geography
d KW: nearest neighbors
d
d Requires: Stata version 17 and Python package eqipop
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260930
d
d Author: John Östh,  Oslo Metropolitan University
d Support: email johnosth@@oslomet.no
d
